flow=[Paragraph('Actual general-function divisors and scope',t),p('<b>Result.</b> Lean proves finite nonzero local orders for every nonzero actual Weierstrass rational function and constructs its actual principal point divisor, product/quotient laws, unit-group additive homomorphism and principal subgroup range. An actual normalized nonconstant F3 function with zero rational-point divisor disproves dropping geometric-point scope from the zero-divisor/constant inference. [pcc:unverified]'),d,Spacer(1,9),p('<b>Finiteness is derived.</b> Actual coordinate evaluation agrees with actual polynomial evaluation. Using the actual rank-two algebra norm formula, evaluation zero implies that the x-coordinate is a root of the actual norm polynomial. The norm is nonzero for a nonzero coordinate function. That polynomial has finitely many roots, and the actual Weierstrass equation has finite monic-quadratic y-fibers in every characteristic. Finite unions/images and an injective actual point-coordinate map give finite affine zero sets. No finite-zero premise is supplied. [pcc:unverified]'),p('<b>Actual local orders and general divisors.</b> A regular function nonvanishing at an actual point is a unit in its actual derived local DVR, hence has official normalized adic value1 and order0. Every actual FunctionField fraction a/b therefore has nonzero point orders only in the finite numerator zero set, denominator zero set and infinity. Lean constructs the Finsupp of these actual normalized local orders and proves product/quotient rules. The actual rational-function unit group maps additively into the actual point-divisor group, with an actual principal subgroup range. This general divisor agrees with the earlier all-n Miller divisors. [pcc:unverified]'),p('<b>Actual rational-only counterexample.</b> On the actual F3 curve y²=x³+x+1, the discriminant is nonzero. The actual function f=(X²+1)/(X²+X+2) is nonzero and differs from every field constant, proved through injectivity of the actual polynomial-function map and coefficient comparison. Both polynomials have no F3 root, so every finite rational-point local order is0. Their actual infinity values are both exp4, giving infinity order0. The difference f−1 has actual value exp(−2), proving leading-residue-one normalization. Thus its actual rational-point divisor is zero despite nonconstancy and normalization. The source uses geometric bar-k points: its qualified constant-kernel statement is not refuted. [pcc:unverified]'),p(f'<b>Checks.</b> Whole tracked project gate {g["declarations"]}/0 failures/0 trusted native, only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound.39modules=33byte-identical credited cores+6new. Complete {binding["full_characters"]}-character binding {binding["full_decl_sha256"]}; native1complete/0prefix/0unresolved. Five snapshots/two failures/three successes, setup/KB/Conductor/protocol retained: {a["files"]}files/{a["unique_objects"]}objects/{size}-byte losslessXZ plus five gate files. Final05/project logs have no warnings/errors; frozen auditor has one inherited String.mk deprecation. No holes/customaxioms/nativeproofeval/raisedlimits/globalflags/waivers/frozenedits/cryptoPython/spend/upload. [pcc:unverified]'),p('<b>Sources and boundaries.</b> Galbraith chapter7 primary281643bytes/21pages/SHA c5b9a25e…: PDF1–2,7–10,13–16 text-read across prior/fresh readings; PDF2,8,9,13,15,16 visually inspected. Fresh PDF13/16 fulltext/visual; Theorem7.7.1 plane proof is the target. Full elliptic7.7.11 proof/Lemma7.7.12 and Cor7.7.13/7.7.14 were read as context after the prior packet issued; they are not formally proved here. Not all21pages read. Exact official norm/root/finite-set/local-unit/fraction/valuation/Finsupp APIs and prior proofs credited; KB/Conductor127, explicit fallback. Actual nonsingularKpoint divisors over arbitraryK include all geometric points only for an elliptic model over algebraically closedK. Geometric degreezero/constantkernel/uniqueness, algebraicclosurebasechange, separate Mathlib Scheme.localRing/Divisor API comparison, translation/reciprocity/isogeny/Lang/Cartier/Jacobian/canonical pairing/MOV-FR/all14 remain open. Same host/prover/Mathlib; procedural header check, signed standing unverified, no novelty/canonical promotion. [pcc:unverified]')]
